<br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T02:01:55-07:00","id":1517255,"title":"","content":"I doubt we'll see any new city sourcebooks in the near future, but I could be wrong. My guess is that you're more likely to see hints of what's taking place in cities via the video games and board games over RPG sourcebooks. An exception <i>could</i> be L.A. based on the popularity of the actual play, but similarly, I imagine Paradox and Renegade are reticent to establish anything in L.A. as canonical fact and then have future productions need to cite them. Anything that requires performers, game designers, and such to reference books is baggage they'd rather not deal with, hence the more toolkit approach to WoD this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T08:08:10-07:00","id":1517275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516235-is-there-any-talks-about-revising-vancouver-by-night-anytime-soon-or-down-the-road?p=1517255#post1517255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt we'll see any new city sourcebooks in the near future, but I could be wrong. My guess is that you're more likely to see hints of what's taking place in cities via the video games and board games over RPG sourcebooks. An exception <i>could</i> be L.A. based on the popularity of the actual play, but similarly, I imagine Paradox and Renegade are reticent to establish anything in L.A. as canonical fact and then have future productions need to cite them. Anything that requires performers, game designers, and such to reference books is baggage they'd rather not deal with, hence the more toolkit approach to WoD this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can work with that and certainly if our characters do make it to Vancouver at any time and we can tweak the setting more to our liking as there were elements that were a pain to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T05:47:13-07:00","id":1517345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516235-is-there-any-talks-about-revising-vancouver-by-night-anytime-soon-or-down-the-road?p=1517255#post1517255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt we'll see any new city sourcebooks in the near future, but I could be wrong. My guess is that you're more likely to see hints of what's taking place in cities via the video games and board games over RPG sourcebooks. An exception <i>could</i> be L.A. based on the popularity of the actual play, but similarly, I imagine Paradox and Renegade are reticent to establish anything in L.A. as canonical fact and then have future productions need to cite them. Anything that requires performers, game designers, and such to reference books is baggage they'd rather not deal with, hence the more toolkit approach to WoD this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes me wonder about New York by Night the liveplay and Coteries visual novels as well.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the information!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T07:12:18-07:00","id":1517351,"title":"","content":"I understand not having city sourcebooks, for me I liked Dark Ages: Europe and Libelus Sanguinis (and Midnight Siege) more than most others. A wider scope, that gives plenty of fertile hooks and plots, without getting into the nitty gritty of a specified locale. Even Transylvania By Night wasn't just Transylvania in the end. <br /> <br /> But I can't deny the lore enthusiast in me would never reject new material on the situation of previous books. Be it new novels, a diary-book (which for me is all those &quot;in-game docs&quot; like book of nod, becketts diary, etc.) or thematic sourcebook with some metaplots.... I always love those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T09:10:47-07:00","id":1517566,"title":"","content":"They'll probably only ever return to city sourcebooks if they're desperate for money and don't have any other ideas to publish. Otherwise it doesn't seem like they're interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T13:52:37-07:00","id":1517655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <d